# Eval engineering

Before marking a coding task complete:

1. Run `node "$GARISEK_OS_ROOT/tools/eval-engineering/cursor-eval.mjs" --root . --fast`
2. On failure: fix or report — do not claim done.
3. Cross-cutting refactors: use `--full` instead of `--fast`.
4. **Floor stations / overlay shell:** after edits to any
   `SCAN_STATION_OVERLAY_COHORT` workspace, run
   `pnpm run eval:station <id>` (see `docs/eval/README.md`). SoT is the
   full cohort — peers, not Pack/Unbox-as-golden. Display eval is
   **slot-table only** — there is no `eval:cohort overlay`. Do not delete
   cohort-law `visibility` / `zIndex.panel` styles to silence critique.
5. **Slot-table cohort (the only display eval):** after CompoundItem /
   `useSlotTableLayout` / PRODUCT_TABLES / DataTable funnel / header-sort
   engine edits, run `pnpm run eval:cohort slot-table`. SoT is engine + every
   product table peer — not To-ship alone. **Hard law:** every painted DATA
   column header is click-to-sort (`SLOT_TABLE_PAINT_LAW.headerSort` /
   `isSlotTableChromeTrack`). Chrome only: select / actions / `_fill` / `thumb`
   (Image photo gutter). Never `sortable: false` on a labeled fact — map the track. Toolbar sort
   menu lists the same facts (`queueColumnSortOptions`); Pick/Status are
   rows, not trigger-only. Cohort `ok`
   fails on tripwire, engine-contract grep, or graph `find` no-match (rebuild
   the cycleforge-app index). Hand-model leftovers:
   `pnpm run eval:discover` — delete only listed DELETE ids; never KEEP rows.
   Orders / To-ship: never remount the shared actions ⋮ (`ordersCompoundColumnsFor` drops `actions`; copy lives on identity chips). KEEP `engine:ordersCompoundColumnsFor`.
   Selecting a row always opens the left Morphing menu on To-ship **and** Shipped (`OrdersGridHost`); gating Morphing on `queueMode === 'fulfillment'` is a cohort fail.
   Header click-to-sort is `?sort=` on every outbound lane — do not pass `sort=` into `OrdersGridHost` (that freeze is a dead-header fork).
6. **Shortcut-display cohort:** after `?` / shortcut / TableStatusBar hotkey
   edits, run `pnpm run eval:cohort shortcuts`. Staff `?` reveals letters
   inline on the buttons. Standing keycaps: refuse. Cheat sheet from the
   table-foot `?`: refuse. No `title`/popover on the question-mark.

Verify commands come from this repo's `package.json` — not model-invented commands.
